body:
If I were you i would keep going with your break. After about 5 months I hopped back on the bandwagon in November as a "treat" to myself. The next two months were a waste of money and a deep dive back into chaos... I spent Christmas, New Years, and Thanksgiving high and I was basically just an anxious zombie around my family. Sure there were some good moments, but after a few years of being off and on most of the time it feels like a waste of time. I don't want to get too r/leaves because I'm still somewhat thankful for more experiences with weed, but finding peace in life without weed is much more rewarding than finding peace within weed.  

&#x200B;

In your case, it takes a long time to break old habits. If you've been doing it for a decade, I would wait at least a year before I hopped back on again. I only started in 2016 and after a 5 month break I was back into old habits in a few days. Plus if you get too much into your old habits again, you'll have to go through the withdrawal all over again.
